.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt SDL3-JSTEST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sdl3-jstest
.Nd test joysticks and gamepads through SDL3
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f | w
.Op Fl Fl geometry Ar W Ns x Ns Ar H
.Op Fl Fl data-dir Ar dir
.Op Ar mode
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the joysticks SDL3 detects, their axes, buttons, hats and balls,
and displays their state or the events they send, the way programs
built with SDL3 see them, instead of reading the raw
.Pa /dev/input
devices.
For devices with a gamepad mapping it also shows the mapped
buttons and axes and where the mapping came from.
.Pp
Without a mode option
.Nm
opens a device menu: in the terminal when built with ncurses,
otherwise in a window.
.Ss Modes
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l , Fl Fl list
List the joysticks and their properties.
.It Fl t Ar JOYNUM , Fl Fl test Ar JOYNUM
Show the state of joystick
.Ar JOYNUM
in the terminal (ncurses builds; otherwise the same as
.Fl Fl gui ) .
.It Fl g Ar JOYNUM , Fl Fl gamecontroller Ar JOYNUM
Show the gamepad state of
.Ar JOYNUM
in the terminal (ncurses builds; otherwise the same as
.Fl Fl gui ) .
.It Fl G , Fl Fl gui Op Ar JOYNUM
Show the device menu in a window, or with
.Ar JOYNUM
that device's state; leaving its view then ends the program.
.It Fl e Ar JOYNUM , Fl Fl event Ar JOYNUM
Print the events received from the joystick until interrupted.
.It Fl r Ar JOYNUM , Fl Fl rumble Ar JOYNUM
Rumble the joystick for three seconds.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl Fl version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl Fl show-paths
Print the data directory and where it was found, then exit.
.El
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl data-dir Ar dir
Read
.Pa gamecontrollerdb.txt
from
.Ar dir .
.It Fl f , Fl Fl fullscreen
Open the window fullscreen.
.It Fl w , Fl Fl windowed
Open the window windowed (the default).
.It Fl Fl geometry Ar W Ns x Ns Ar H
Window size; the default is 640x480.
The display is scaled to the window with its aspect ratio kept.
.El
.Sh WINDOW CONTROLS
In the menu, the arrow keys move, Enter opens a device and Esc quits;
a mouse click or a tap opens a row, the last row quits.
On a gamepad the D-pad or left stick moves, A or Start opens and B or
Back quits.
.Pp
A device view is left with Esc, the Android Back key, the
.Dq Menu
button at the top right, or by holding the gamepad's Back / Select
button for one second, so that every other button stays testable.
Ctrl-C quits everywhere.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG , Ev SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG_FILE
Extra controller mappings, read by SDL; the startup report says which
source each device's mapping came from.
.It Ev SDL_VIDEODRIVER
The video driver.
Without a usable display the terminal modes fall back to
.Dq dummy .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa gamecontrollerdb.txt
Controller mappings in the data directory: the
.Fl Fl data-dir
option, else
.Pa ../share/sdl-jstest
relative to the executable, else the install prefix.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when SDL or the window cannot be initialised, 2 on
invalid command line options.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
At startup
.Nm
prints a report to standard error: version, build, system, SDL
environment variables, the SDL library in use, the video and renderer
drivers and every joystick
with its GUID and mapping source.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jstest 1 ,
.Xr jstest-gtk 1 ,
.Xr sdl1-jstest 1 ,
.Xr sdl2-jstest 1
